local config = {
  str_guide_link_warn = "Follow the path to defeat the enemy",
  str_guide_warn_desc1 = "Do you still remember how to use Chain Combo?",
  str_guide_pop_title = "Chain Combo",
  str_guide_pop_desc = [[
Once a chain reaches <color=#ff8f3d>a certain length</color>, it will <color=#ff8f3d>automatically trigger a Chain Combo</color>.
Generally, <color=#ff8f3d>the longer the connection</color>, <color=#ff8f3d>the more powerful</color> the Chain Combo.
Every Aurorian's Chain Combo has different effects and trigger conditions, so mix and match as you see fit!]],
  str_guide_pop_close = "Close",
  str_guide_pop_extra = "Tips: Using Chain Combo to pierce through the whole battlefield is the most important ability of Aurorians.",
  str_guide_condition_finish = "<color=#9db4ff>Completed %s</color>",
  str_guide_condition_nofinish = "<color=#fa8892>Incomplete %s</color>",
  str_guide_pop_title_lineskill = "Chain Combo",
  str_guide_pop_desc_lineskill = [[
Once a chain reaches <color=#ff8f3d>a certain length</color>, it will <color=#ff8f3d>automatically trigger a Chain Combo</color>.
Generally, <color=#ff8f3d>the longer the connection</color>, <color=#ff8f3d>the more powerful</color> the Chain Combo.
Every Aurorian's Chain Combo has different effects and trigger conditions, so mix and match as you see fit!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_lineskill = "An Aurorian's true worth comes from what she displays beyond her power.\n                                      —Reinhardt's Message III—",
  str_guide_pop_title_moreline = "Multi-Aurorian Connection",
  str_guide_pop_desc_moreline = [[
When multiple Aurorians are deployed, only those with the same element as the tiles in the chain will act.
<color=#ff5f51>Red tiles</color> will activate <color=#ff5f51>Fire</color> Aurorians, and <color=#6fd5ff>Blue tiles</color> will activate <color=#6fd5ff>Water</color> Aurorians.
<color=#85ff3b>Green tiles</color> will activate <color=#85ff3b>Forest</color> Aurorians, and <color=#fee039>Yellow tiles</color> will activate <color=#fee039>Thunder</color> Aurorians.
Don't worry, Captain Aurorians will <color=#ff8f3d>ignore tile elements</color> and act every round.]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_moreline = "The world is blessed by the Goddess, who fills one's heart with Light.\n                                      —Reinhardt's Message I—",
  str_guide_pop_title_mainskill1 = "Active Skill",
  str_guide_pop_desc_mainskill1 = [[
Active Skills are divided into Preemptive Strike Skills and Non-preemptive Strike Skills. <color=#ff8f3d>Preemptive Strike Skills</color> can be used right when the battle begins!
Active Skills must <color=#ff8f3d>be used before connection</color>, and <color=#ff8f3d>will enter a cooldown period</color> after use.
Different Aurorians have different Active Skills, and the right combination of different skills can yield tremendous benefits!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_mainskill1 = "The stretch of time has sown seeds of dispute in our hearts, yet it has also nurtured magnificent wonders.\n                                      —Reinhardt's Message II—",
  str_guide_pop_title_mainskill2 = "Tile-Converting Skill",
  str_guide_pop_desc_mainskill2 = [[
The tile-converting skill is able to <color=#ff8f3d>convert certain tiles</color> and change the <color=#ff8f3d>Alchemy Board</color>.
Tile-converting will bring about more <color=#ff8f3d>possibilities for chains</color> and is the strongest support skill.
Use tile-converting at the right time to execute your strategy for a turnaround!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_mainskill2 = "The only thing that never changes is change itself.\n                                      —Reinhardt's Message IV—",
  str_guide_pop_title_levelup = "Upgrade",
  str_guide_pop_desc_levelup = "Level up and amass Aurorian power",
  str_guide_pop_extra_levelup = "Level Description XXX",
  str_guide_pop_title_lineskillrange = "Chain Combo Range",
  str_guide_pop_desc_lineskillrange = [[
Confirming the range of a Chain Combo is the most basic way to increase combat efficiency.
The range of your Aurorians' different skills varies. <color=#ff8f3d>Don't lift your finger</color> after connecting, and you'll be able to <color=#ff8f3d>preview</color> the range of every skill.
<color=#ff8f3d>Adjusting the endpoint of the chain</color> will change the area the Aurorian's skill affects. This is super important!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_lineskillrange = "The greatest honor among comrades is to trust one another with one's life.\n                                      —Reinhardt's Message VII—",
  str_guide_pop_title_leaderskill = "Captain Skill",
  str_guide_pop_desc_leaderskill = "Some Aurorians have a special Passive Skill that surpasses other Aurorians, that is the Captain Skill!",
  str_guide_pop_extra_leaderskill = "The Captain Skill is very rare and can significantly boost the abilities of Aurorians with the same element.",
  str_guide_pop_title_jiguan = "Trap",
  str_guide_pop_desc_jiguan = [[
Flame Traps will <color=#ff8f3d>rotate regularly</color>, dealing damage to targets in <color=#ff8f3d>rows or columns</color>.
Traps may <color=#ff8f3d>attack us</color> or <color=#ff8f3d>our enemies</color>, and can work wonders if used effectively.
Try to stay out of their attack range and be careful not to let the traps block your connection!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_jiguan = "There was a lot of junk in the olden days, but a lot of... interesting stuffs as well! Isn't that right?\n                                      —Gronru's Observation Diary—",
  str_guide_pop_title_muchaoguai = "Brood Monster",
  str_guide_pop_desc_muchaoguai = [[
Brood Monsters <color=#ff8f3d>cannot move</color>, but will <color=#ff8f3d>continuously summon Eclipsites</color>. 
If you fail to defeat them in time, the battlefield will be swarming with enemies.
<color=#ff8f3d>Directly attacking the monster itself</color> is the best way to deal with it, especially against medium-sized monsters.
And don't say I didn't warn you: <color=#ff8f3d>Beating them with area attacks is the way to go</color>!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_muchaoguai = "Some Eclipsites are really gross. When torn apart, there's gooey... (Data Deleted)\n                                      —Gronru's Observation Diary—",
  str_guide_pop_title_shenyuan = "Abyssal Tile",
  str_guide_pop_desc_shenyuan = "Abyssal tiles cannot be crossed, but flying monsters can pass through, so can you via teleportation.",
  str_guide_pop_extra_shenyuan = "Can pass through via teleportation.",
  str_guide_pop_title_moredamge = "Eclipsite Body Types and Damage",
  str_guide_pop_desc_moredamge = [[
Eclipsites have a variety of <color=#ff8f3d>sizes</color>, and the most common ones are single tile Eclipsites.
There are Quadriune Eclipsites and even larger Eclipsites that exist, although they are huge and strong, they are more vulnerable to damage in battle.
<color=#ff8f3d>Since they occupy multiple tiles, they will take damage multiple times from area attacks </color>as well as chain attacks!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_moredamge = "The bigger the enemy, the easier it is to deal with it. Just close your eyes and beat them up.\n                                      —Quotes From Barton (unpublished)—",
  str_guide_pop_title_leveltask = "Stage Quest",
  str_guide_pop_desc_leveltask = "There are many types of Stage Quests, and you can clear the stage by completing them",
  str_guide_pop_extra_leveltask = "Clear the stage by completing Stage Quests",
  str_guide_pop_title_escape = "Escape Point",
  str_guide_pop_desc_escape = [[
The Escape Point is a feature through which you can clear a special stage. By <color=#ff8f3d>moving to a specific tile</color>, you can instantly claim victory.
Note that the Escape Point is <color=#ff8f3d>locked</color> initially and can only be unlocked by meeting certain conditions.
There are many unlock conditions, such as <color=#ff8f3d>collecting items or defeating Eclipsites</color>.]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_escape = "There is no shame in running away. These temporary retreats are for the sake of greater ambitions...\n                                      —Letters from Sharona—",
  str_guide_pop_title_monsterinfo = "View Details",
  str_guide_pop_desc_monsterinfo = [[
<color=#ff8f3d>Tap and hold the tile beneath the monster's feet</color> to see its attack range and other details.
Keeping an eye on the opponent's traits will make you undefeatable!]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_monsterinfo = "If you know yourself and know your enemies, you will never be defeated. \n                                      —Old Unknown Tome, Incomplete Excerpt—",
  str_guide_pop_title_jiguangshike = "Aurora Time",
  str_guide_pop_desc_jiguangshike = [[
Once a chain <color=#ff8f3d>reaches 15 tiles</color>, Aurora Time will be triggered, and you will gain an extra chance to act.
During Aurora Time, Aurorians can use their prepared Active Skills and can also trigger their Chain Combos through another chain.
Aurora Time <color=#ff8f3d>can only be triggered once per round</color>, bringing you great benefits in battle.]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_jiguangshike = "We only know bits and pieces about the magic power of Light.\n                                      —Old Unknown Tome, Incomplete Excerpt—",
  str_guide_pop_title_jianglihuihe = "Bonus Time",
  str_guide_pop_desc_jianglihuihe = [[
Enter Bonus Time by clearing stages in White Night, Black Underbelly at a certain difficulty level a specific number of times.
There will be multiple Corrupted Eclipsites on the battlefield, and defeating them will earn you extra Nightium!
Note that their <color=#ff8f3d>ACT is very high</color>, which enables them to evade our attacks.]],
  str_guide_pop_extra_jianglihuihe = "Lucky moments may come once every day!\n      —White Night, Black Underbelly: A Guide—",
